    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2KPRRzem8yYfc5PawUUApJv)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Based on `main` at `ba368f27` (after #497 and #499); independent of the open PRs.\n- Docs of the DEVONthink modules are also touched by #419 (open, moves them to `docs/tangles/devonthink/`); whichever merges second resolves the moved/deleted `sp-devonthink-search.org`.\n- The history entries in the docs name this PR as #500.\n- Branch is `claude/project-thread-rex2wj`: the cloud proxy cannot create the number-prefixed branch, so it needs the prefix from Sia.\n\n## What changed\n\n- `sp-devonthink-browse` and `sp-devonthink-search` did the same job (same candidates, category and Embark actions; pick a record and open it), so they are now one module and one command.\n- Module `sp-devonthink-browse` (`.el`, doc, tests) now holds everything; `sp-devonthink-search` (module, doc, tests) is removed and no longer required by `sp-academic`. No shims.\n- Command `sp-devonthink-browse` (`C-; k d f`):\n  - empty query: the record list, grouped by DEVONthink group, cached;\n  - a query: DEVONthink search; `C-u` chooses the engine (DEVONthink or litdb);\n  - empty query with a litdb engine: `user-error \"litdb needs a query\"`.\n- Also moved in: `sp-devonthink-similar`, `-similar-to-note` (`C-; k d a`), `sp-devonthink-preview`, and Embark `s` and `v`.\n- Renamed:\n  - options `sp-devonthink-search-limit` and `-preview-chars` are now `sp-devonthink-browse-limit` and `-preview-chars`;\n  - the internal `sp-devonthink-search--*` functions are now `sp-devonthink-browse--*` (the rank-ordered table is `--ranked-table`).\n- Removed: the key `C-; k d b` (the old `sp-devonthink-browse` command was the same as `C-; k d f` with an empty query).\n- Docs (bullets): the two pages are merged into `sp-devonthink-browse.org` (history entries for #415, #418, #453, #454, #500); `sp-devonthink.org`, `sp-fetch-inbox.org`, `sp-academic.org` and `README.org` updated. `CHANGELOG.org` not edited.\n- Tests: the search tests are in `tests/sp-devonthink-browse-test.el` (renamed), plus new ones: empty query browses, litdb with empty query errors, merged command and keys.\n\n## Not done or not checked\n\n- No Emacs in the container: the tests and `tools/check-tangle.sh` were not run. I checked by script that the `emacs-lisp` blocks of the doc equal the `.el` (ignoring blank lines) and that the parentheses balance.\n- The DEVONthink JavaScript is unchanged.\n- The key stays `f` (not `b`); say if you want `C-; k d b` for browse.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [ ] `C-; k d f`, press `RET` on an empty query: the record list appears, grouped by DEVONthink group; choosing one opens it in DEVONthink.\n- [ ] `C-; k d f`, type a query (e.g. `kind:pdf value form`): ranked hits with kind and page count, as before.\n- [ ] `C-u C-; k d f`, choose a litdb engine, type a query: litdb search runs; with an empty query you get \"litdb needs a query\".\n- [ ] Embark on a record from either list: `o p n l t s v` work (`y` and `f` too, from bibsync and fetch-inbox).\n- [ ] `C-; k d a` in a litnote lists similar records.\n- [ ] `C-; k d b` is unbound; `M-x sp-devonthink-search` does not exist; Emacs starts with no error about a missing `sp-devonthink-search`.\n- [ ] `M-x sp-devonthink-browse-refresh`, then `C-; k d f` + `RET`: the new list is shown.\n- [ ] `M-x ert` with `sp-devonthink`: all pass.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9s57TjxKDkAZRDQUU)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9s57TjxKDkAZRDQUU",
